  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper trough in NW flow has moved into the area, and is most\nprominent over the far east. According to the latest NBM, there\nare showers expected to linger through at least Friday evening\nbefore pushing east. There is a decent chance of isolated \nthunderstorms pushing across the central and western parts of the \narea this afternoon, but little in the way of accumulation or \nstrong winds is expected. There is a low to moderate end \nopportunity for wetting rain amounts in the southeast through \nFriday evening (10 to 40 percent).\n\nOn Friday into the holiday weekend, an upper level ridge will \nbuild in to bring mostly clear and warm to hot conditions as high \nas the 90s on Memorial Day. Ensemble cluster analyses differ on \nthunderstorm chances associated with some breakdown of the ridge \nby the middle of next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nIncreased winds and PoPs for this afternoon to reflect CAMs.\n\nConfidence is moderate for thunderstorms today in the central and\nwestern parts of the area.\n\nThere is high confidence in the upper trough lingering through\nFriday evening in the east.\n\nThere is low to moderate confidence of wetting rain amounts\noccurring in the southeast through Friday evening.",
